      "question": {
        "questionText": "Three coins are available: \\(C_1\\) is a two-headed coin, \\(C_2\\) is a biased coin with \\(P(H\\mid C_2)=75\\%\\), and \\(C_3\\) is an unbiased coin. A coin is selected according to the following data and tossed once.\\n\\n| Coin | \\(P(C_i)\\) | \\(P(H\\mid C_i)\\) |\\n|---|---:|---:|\\n| \\(C_1\\) | \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) | \\(1\\) |\\n| \\(C_2\\) | \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) | \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) |\\n| \\(C_3\\) | \\(\\frac{3}{10}\\) | \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) |\\n\\nIf the outcome is observed to be a head, \\(H\\), then the probability that the selected coin was \\(C_2\\) is",
        "equationLatex": "\\(P(C_2\\mid H)=\\frac{P(C_2)P(H\\mid C_2)}{P(C_1)P(H\\mid C_1)+P(C_2)P(H\\mid C_2)+P(C_3)P(H\\mid C_3)}\\)",
